Homework 2 CS 511 -

Topics: Thread Pools, Semaphores, Java Executor, CountDownLatch, ExecutorService

This homework was a fun assignment to work on and taught me about the practical use of sempahores.

The assignment was about managing shared resources in a bakery implemented in OOP style in Java. The bakery had 3 shelves with different types of bread and 4 cashiers. Customers were able to go in and buy bread, but only 1 customer was allowed at each shelf and cashier; the thread pool consisted of 200 customers with 50 in the store at once.

There was a main function that called Bakery's thread which created a thread pool and created threads for each customer. The bakery held semaphores to control each shelf and cashier.

Very fun indeed!
